Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: RHACS Operator Installation Fails
Symptoms:

Operator pods in CrashLoopBackOff state
CSV shows failed status
Solution:

# Check operator logs
oc logs -n stackrox deployment/rhacs-operator-controller-manager

# Verify sufficient resources
oc describe nodes | grep -A 5 "Allocated resources"

# Clean up and reinstall if necessary
oc delete subscription rhacs-operator -n stackrox
oc delete csv -n stackrox --all
# Wait 2 minutes, then reinstall
Issue 2: Central UI Not Accessible
Symptoms:

Route exists but UI returns 503 error
Central pods not ready
Solution:

# Check Central pod status
oc get pods -n stackrox | grep central

# Check Central logs
oc logs -n stackrox deployment/central

# Verify route configuration
oc get route central -n stackrox -o yaml

# Check service endpoints
oc get endpoints central -n stackrox
Issue 3: Scanner Not Working
Symptoms:

Images not being scanned
Scanner pods failing
Solution:

# Check scanner pod logs
oc logs -n stackrox deployment/scanner

# Verify scanner configuration
oc get central stackrox-central-services -n stackrox -o yaml | grep -A 10 scanner

# Restart scanner if needed
oc rollout restart deployment/scanner -n stackrox
Issue 4: Admission Controller Blocking Deployments
Symptoms:

All deployments being rejected
Admission controller too restrictive
Solution:

# Check admission controller logs
oc logs -n stackrox deployment/admission-control

# Temporarily disable enforcement
oc patch securedcluster stackrox-secured-cluster-services -n stackrox --type='merge' -p='{"spec":{"admissionControl":{"enforceOnCreates":false}}}'

# Review and adjust policies in RHACS UI
